<https://dgg32.github.io/glp/ontology#TherapeuticClass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A concept in the therapeutic class scheme (e.g. SGLT2 inhibitors). The hierarchy itself is maintained as a SKOS concept scheme, not as OWL subclasses."@en .
<https://dgg32.github.io/glp/ontology#pseudonymousId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The source data is public and names the prescribers, so a determined reader could still re-identify someone by matching claim counts. The pseudonym keeps names and NPIs out of the graph, demos and screenshots; it is not anonymization."@en .
<https://dgg32.github.io/glp/ontology/imports/idmp-o-1.4.0-extract> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology> .
<https://dgg32.github.io/glp/ontology#hasActiveSubstance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Shortcut for the IDMP-O pattern product -hasActiveIngredient-> ActiveIngredient role -isPlayedBy-> Substance. The property chain makes data modelled the IDMP-O way also answer queries that use this shortcut."@en .
<https://dgg32.github.io/glp/ontology#total30DayFills> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .
